0. Definitions
   "Software": CloudTerm (desktop and Android), its source code, binaries,
   installers, documentation and assets included in this repository.
   "Author": pilahito (DavidPilahito7), the copyright holder.
   "You": any individual or legal entity that obtains the Software.

1. What you MAY do (free of charge)
   a) Download, install and USE the Software, for personal use and for internal
      or professional use (including within a company), at no cost.
   b) View and read the source code to study, audit or verify its security.
   c) Build the unmodified source code solely for your own use, without
      distributing the result.

2. What you may NOT do without the Author's prior written permission
   a) Modify the Software or create derivative works (published forks, adapted
      versions, reusing parts of the code in another product).
   b) Redistribute copies of the Software, modified or unmodified, by any means
      (websites, mirror repositories, packages, torrents, etc.).
   c) Publish the Software or versions based on it in app stores (Google Play,
      App Store, Microsoft Store, F-Droid, Snap, Flathub or others).
   d) Sell, rent, sublicense or charge in any way for the Software, or offer it
      as a paid service (SaaS, hosting, etc.).
   e) Remove or alter copyright notices or this license.
   Permission requests go through GitHub: https://github.com/pilahito

3. Trademark, name and logo
   The name "CloudTerm", its logo and icons belong to the Author. This license
   grants no right to use them, except to truthfully refer to the original
   Software. No other project may use them to present itself as CloudTerm or
   as related to it.

4. Contributions
   Contributions via pull requests to the official repository are welcome. By
   submitting a contribution you state that you have the right to do so and
   grant the Author a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free, irrevocable and
   transferable license to use, modify, sublicense and distribute that
   contribution as part of the Software, under this or any other license.
   Preparing a contribution in your local copy for that sole purpose is
   permitted.

5. Third-party components
   The Software includes third-party libraries, fonts and assets under their
   own licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, MPL-2.0, ISC, OFL-1.1, etc.). Those
   components are governed by their respective licenses, which this license
   does not limit.

6. Earlier versions
   Versions of the Software released before this license change were
   distributed under the GNU AGPL-3.0-or-later. Anyone who obtained those
   versions keeps, with respect to them, the rights granted by the AGPL-3.0.
   This license applies to all versions released after the change.

7. No warranty
   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
   IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
   FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE
   AUTHOR BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN
